36
00:07:54.891 --> 00:07:57.268
Best practices for getting started with Claude.

37
00:07:57.718 --> 00:08:03.097
Below, I share tips and tricks inspired by my own experience working with Claude Code:

38
00:08:03.547 --> 00:08:23.321
1. Start small, with something you already do manually. It can be hard to get started when there’s so much noise about what people are doing with A I. My advice: pick the repetitive task you spend the most hands-on time on and ask Claude to rebuild it. That way, you’ll be able to judge the output because you already know what good looks like.

39
00:08:23.441 --> 00:08:36.070
If the problem still feels too big, use Claude as a thought partner to break it into steps. And if it’s something you share with other people, route the early runs to yourself first so you catch the errors before anyone else does.

40
00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:54.545
2. Write instructions in plain language and version each document. Brief Claude the way you’d brief a new colleague and Claude will do the rest. Instruct Claude to save each update as a numbered version with a one-line note of what’s changed, so you have a record of the prompts that produced each past run.

41
00:08:54.665 --> 00:09:04.295
Ours is a markdown file my colleagues run for their own segments; we started from a shared Google Doc and moved to GitHub once more people needed to edit it.

42
00:09:04.535 --> 00:09:22.878
3. Pilot with a small, committed group. We ran our first tests with a handful of account executives who we knew would be willing to spend the time on providing us feedback and improving the report over time, helping us detect errors or offer suggestions on how to expand or personalize coverage.

43
00:09:23.118 --> 00:09:37.198
4. Use feedback to improve your prompt, fold in each correction as an explicit rule. The marketing briefing became useful when the recipients started sharing feedback with us and each correction became an explicit rule for Claude.

44
00:09:37.648 --> 00:09:54.111
Claude automated a manual process that used to take me hours each Sunday, but with this project, my team and I have gained something much better than time: our output is now more personal, more useful, and more measurable. What marketing process can you improve with Claude?

45
00:09:54.561 --> 00:09:56.343
Get started with Claude Code today.

